// Title: Potential ACTINIUM Persistence Activity
// Sigma ID: e1118a8f-82f5-44b3-bb6b-8a284e5df602
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Andreas Hunkeler (@Karneades)
// Date: 2022-02-07 | Modified: 2023-03-18
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, persistence, T1053, T1053.005
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects specific process parameters as used by ACTINIUM scheduled task persistence creation.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/02/04/actinium-targets-ukrainian-organizations
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2022/TA/ACTINIUM/proc_creation_win_apt_actinium_persistence.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "schtasks" and ProcessCommandLine contains "create" and ProcessCommandLine contains "wscript" and ProcessCommandLine contains " /e:vbscript"
